<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 223 0 R
/E (Shaun Woods is a Lehigh County resident and working father of two. In 2018, he was convicted of manufacturing with intent to deliver, his first adult felony conviction. He received work release and completed his supervision.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
490 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 223 0 R
/E (Years later, the conviction continued to follow him into the housing market. When Woods attempted to add his name to an apartment lease, he says management told him its policy prohibited someone with a drug selling conviction from living there. He eventually moved out and began looking for landlords willing to consider more than his past.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
491 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 223 0 R
/E (Today, Woods' two sons live with him, making stable housing even more important. In 2026, he finally found a leasing agent who listened to his circumstances and approved a larger apartment in his own name.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
