/E (Tara Bruno is a Philadelphia resident, mother of two, and first-generation college graduate. After earning her GED, she attended community college, received a full scholarship to college and ultimately earned bachelor's and master's degrees.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
517 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 224 0 R
/E (After her marriage ended, Bruno says she entered an abusive relationship with a man involved with drugs. She describes a relationship marked by violence and threats against her and her children. In 2017, that turbulent period of her life culminated in a felony conviction for possession with intent to distribute.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
518 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 224 0 R
/E (Nearly a decade later, Bruno says that conviction still shapes where she can live. She has experienced landlords rejecting her after background checks and has relied on small landlords, additional deposits, and a cosigner to secure housing. )
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
