543 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 225 0 R
/E (Because of the difficulty in measuring discrimination in the behavior of landlords, lenders, and other actors, it is impossible to know the true extent to which Pennsylvanians are denied housing under Thurmond. The counts presented in this report estimate the total number of Pennsylvanians who are potentially impacted due to a past drug selling or manufacturing conviction. However, it is unknown what proportion of these individuals have experienced explicit denial of housing specifically due to these convictions.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
544 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 225 0 R
/E (Further, available state-level court data for drug selling convictions only dates back to 2007 and only includes Pennsylvania convictions, so individuals with convictions occurring prior to 2007 or in neighboring states will not be included in the counts. This means we are not able to capture the full impact of the Thurmond Amendment, which has been federal law since 1988.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
