/E (Individuals convicted of Thurmond-eligible charges have been recorded as living in every county in Pennsylvania. The following figures illustrate counts and characteristics of people convicted of such charges from 2007-2025. )
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
581 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 227 0 R
/E (Statewide, there were an estimated 91,664 people convicted of drug selling or manufacturing charges, an average of roughly 4,824 people each year. Of people with Thurmond eligible convictions, 34% received those convictions in Philadelphia courts. While the number of defendants with a first-known conviction has fluctuated year-to-year, total new people with Thurmond-eligible convictions decreased from 2007 to 2019. New convictions dropped dramatically during the COVID-19 pandemic, and despite increasing in recent years, still remain below pre-COVID levels. This downward trend may represent changes in drug selling behavior or changes to policing, prosecution, and court practices and priorities. It may also be due in part to limitations in the data time period mentioned above.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
