/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 228 0 R
/E (As the most populous county in the state, Philadelphia accounts for the largest total count and proportion of Pennsylvania convictions compared to any other individual county. Across the study time period, Philadelphia county also experienced the largest and most marked decline in these types of convictions. Looking forward from 2007, first-known, Thurmond-eligible convictions peaked in Philadelphia in 2011 at 4,303 cases, with a steep decline between 2014 and 2020. While case totals rose again in the county and statewide, they remain below 2019 totals. )
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [1]
>>
