606 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 228 0 R
/E (We also examined the proportion of defendants convicted of an eligible offense by calculating the rate of those convicted per 100,000 residents in each county. When accounting for population, Blair County in central Pennsylvania had the highest rate of defendants with eligible offenses with 4,462 per 100,000 residents, or about 2% of the county population. This points to a significant drug supply problem in the county, and its toll is reflected in public health data. Sadly, according to the Pennsylvania Department of Health, the per capita rate of drug-related overdose deaths in Blair County has steadily increased since 2018.)
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [4]
>>
