/P 231 0 R
/E (Based on available data, the median age at first known, Thurmond-eligible conviction in Pennsylvania was 30 years old, and over a third \(36%\), of defendants had a first-known conviction at ages 25 or younger. While this falls in line with typical age-crime curves where younger people are more represented in crime statistics, age may also skew slightly older due to data limitations mentioned above. The proportion of defendants continued to decrease as age at first conviction increases. )
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [2]
