/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 236 0 R
/E (Defendants charged with Thurmond-eligible charges were most frequently represented by just public defenders \(38% of defendants had a public defender\). A quarter of defendants had private counsel \(25%\) for the duration of their case. Just over a quarter \(27%\) of defendants had more than one representation type over the course of their case. The rest \(10%\) of the defendants had court-appointed counsel. )
/Pg 33 0 R
/K [3]
>>
