857 0 obj
<<
/Title (To understand the association between representation type and likelihood of conviction, we measured the conviction rate just for defendants who had one type of representation throughout the life of their case. Defendants who could afford private counsel were convicted of Thurmond eligible charges in a less than half \(45%\) of cases. Defendants who relied solely on publicly provided counsel fared just slightly worse, experiencing convictions about half of the time \(49-51% across both types\).  From the data, it is unclear whether the relatively small differences in conviction rates are related to the differences in representation or other case or defendant characteristics.)
