<<
/Title (Available data do not include Hispanic/Latinx ethnicity \(only race\), and records only binary sex categories \(not gender\). Therefore, it is unknown whether any Latinx defendants were convicted of drug selling charges in this period. It is also unknown whether there were any defendants who identified as something other than male or female. Finally, it is unknown if all these defendants identified within the data are still alive or still living in the Commonwealth. Despite these limitations this analysis of Pennsylvania data is still an important accounting of how the Thurmond Amendment potentially affects Pennsylvania, the fifth-largest state in the US.)
